From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patchset <patchset@localhost>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:15:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 34/43] minimize: focused window item gets a solid background,
 colours in a file

At alpha 0.25 a dark accent (e.g. #004E8C) on the dark panel blends into a
murky colour that does not read as the accent. The focused item is now
filled opaque: by default the accent mixed 30 % toward black, with the
title and second row in the text colour of the theme's accent buttons
(second row at 75 %, as before). The theme's on-accent colour is not used:
the dark theme sets it to black. Unfocused items are unchanged.

~/.config/minimize-ws/colors sets them (re-read on change like the other
files): focused_bg (system or #RRGGBB), focused_darken (0 to 1) and
focused_text (system or #RRGGBB). An invalid value is logged and that key
keeps its default.

